On your question about mixed `round_idx` values inside one `all_findings` bucket: that is a real malformed-checkpoint edge case. A fallback keyed by `rnd[0].round_idx` would be unsafe because it silently aliases heterogeneous findings into one round. The fail-closed correction is to validate homogeneity before reconstruction and reject inconsistent buckets instead of inferring identity from the first element.

